-- Step BI-1: the four Configuration 4-7 combination flush casement templates.
-- Run by the reviewer in the Supabase SQL editor. Safe to re-run.
--
-- Nathan (15 Oct 2026): all four of these layouts are sold. They are
-- Integrate's own templates from DrawingBoard Config, CW family, group
-- "3. Combination Flush Casements"
-- (docs/integrate-L31115-configurations-4-7.txt, read 15 Oct by the reviewer
-- on L31115 item 10, drawings 29-32):
--
--    89818  Configuration 4   1299 x 1307   opener | fixed | opener
--    89819  Configuration 5   1699 x 1307   opener | fixed | fixed | opener
--     6601  Configuration 6   1499 x 1199   a full-height opener each side and
--                                           a top-hung fanlight over a fixed
--                                           sash in the MIDDLE column
--     6602  Configuration 7   1499 x 1199   three columns, a light over each
--
-- Integrate's names are "Configuration 4 / 5 / 6 / 7", which say nothing about
-- the layout in a template list, so each name here describes the window and
-- keeps Integrate's name in brackets — the convention sql/step-av1 set for
-- Configurations 1-3. The group name is Integrate's own without its leading
-- number, as those four have.
--
-- SORT ORDER 72-78, so the seven Configurations sit together and in order
-- after "Fanlight Over Fixed With Full-Height Opener (Configuration 3)" at 70.
-- Nothing already in the table is renumbered: 80 and 90 are the two French
-- casements (sql/step-ax2) and they stay where they are. If the reviewer would
-- rather these ran 100-130 after the French pair, only the four sort_order
-- values below change — nothing else in this script depends on them.
--
-- GEOMETRY. Every tree below was GENERATED by the board's own code
-- (scripts/build-step-bi-sql.mjs, from COMBINATION_CASEMENT_TEMPLATES in
-- src/drawingBoard/combinationCasement.js), so each template is exactly what
-- the board builds: buildCasementFrame at Integrate's size, the transom /
-- mullion picker, then — for Configuration 6 — the picker's second mode (a
-- divider in ONE column, which stores startDivider / endDivider as Integrate
-- does), then the operation buttons and the fanlight bottom rails. The board's
-- pickers lay out EQUAL columns; Integrate's templates do not, so Integrate's
-- own stored offsets are written onto the dividers, which is what a surveyor
-- does when they type an offset after picking a grid.
--
-- The cells that come out are Integrate's, cell for cell — asserted against
-- the TC4-TC7 benchmark fixtures in src/drawingBoard/combinationCasement.test.js:
--
--    89818  1299 x 1307  interior 1225 x 1213  columns 393 | 385 | 393
--                        A1 393x1213  B1 385x1213  C1 393x1213
--    89819  1699 x 1307  interior 1625 x 1213  columns 389 | 383 | 383 | 389
--                        A1 389  B1 383  C1 383  D1 389, all 1213 high
--     6601  1499 x 1199  interior 1425 x 1105  columns 459 | 451 | 461
--                        A1 459x1105 (spans both rows), B1 451x356 (the
--                        fanlight), C1 461x1105 (spans), B2 451x722
--     6602  1499 x 1199  interior 1425 x 1105  a 3 x 2 grid
--                        top 459/451/461 x 356, bottom the same widths x 722
--
-- CONFIGURATION 6'S TRANSOM IS SHORT, and bounded at BOTH ends: its
-- startDivider is the left mullion and its endDivider the right one, so it
-- exists in the middle column alone. It is the first divider in GlazePro
-- bounded at both ends. `drawing_parts` has no key column, so those two
-- references are re-pointed to the row ids after every save
-- (src/drawingBoard/dividerRefs.js, Step BH follow-up 2); the round trip is
-- tested on this very template in src/drawingBoard/saveRoundTrip.test.js. If
-- a reference were lost the frame would read as a 3 x 2 grid of six cells
-- instead of four, which is the £1,832.54 that went missing on live
-- drawings 56 and 60.
--
-- NATHAN'S DECISIONS, the same four as Configurations 1-3:
--
--  * BOTTOM RAILS. A fanlight's rail is 62 and an ordinary casement's 83
--    (12 Oct; sql/step-as0 holds casementSashPart.bottomHeight 83 and
--    casementSashPart.defaultFanlightBottomHeight 62). A fanlight is a
--    top-row sash that does NOT run the full height, read from the CELLS —
--    so Configuration 6 has exactly ONE 62 (its middle light; the two
--    spanning openers keep 83) and Configuration 7 has three, its whole top
--    row. Configurations 4 and 5 are single rows: nothing in them is a
--    fanlight and every rail is 83. Integrate's own templates store 83
--    everywhere, the fanlights included; the benchmark fixtures keep
--    Integrate's 83 as recorded and these templates do not.
--
--  * NO STORED SURROUND LIST, so no nosing (sql/step-ax3's decision carried
--    forward). Integrate recalculates the surround on the first save and
--    never produces a nosing, so carrying one would make every GlazePro
--    drawing one component line and 30 minutes of install labour (rule 251
--    "Windowboard") dearer than the same drawing in Integrate. A new drawing
--    prices its surround through the allocator — architrave only.
--
--  * NO STORED IRONMONGERY LIST: the default_ironmongery rules price it and
--    follow the openings (difference 4 in docs/integrate-differences.md).
--
--  * Casement MPLS on, Solid Redwood frame and sashes, utile cill, complete
--    new, Clean White both sides.
--
-- Product and Quantity are both is_required (Step AQ), so the product code is
-- looked up BY LABEL — the product reference list came from Integrate and its
-- codes are not in the repository — and the script fails loudly rather than
-- writing a code that would look set and still fail the check.
--
-- RUN SECTION 0 FIRST.

-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- SECTION 0 — read before changing
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

-- 0a. The profile. Expect ONE active row, code 'casement'.
SELECT id, code, is_active FROM public.default_profiles WHERE code = 'casement';

-- 0b. The two profile values the 62 / 83 rails depend on. Expect
--     casementSashPart.bottomHeight 83 and
--     casementSashPart.defaultFanlightBottomHeight 62. If bottomHeight is
--     MISSING, sql/step-as0 has not run: STOP and run it first, or every rail
--     in a new drawing will come out 62.
SELECT v.field_key, v.default_value
FROM   public.default_profile_values v
JOIN   public.default_profiles p ON p.id = v.profile_id
WHERE  p.code = 'casement'
  AND  v.field_key IN ('casementSashPart.bottomHeight',
                       'casementSashPart.defaultFanlightBottomHeight')
ORDER  BY v.field_key;

-- 0c. The containment these need. Expect rows for assemblyFramePart ->
--     casementSashPart / mullionPart / transomPart / cillPart, and
--     casementSashPart -> glassPart.
SELECT parent_code, child_code, min_count, max_count
FROM   public.part_type_children
WHERE  (parent_code = 'assemblyFramePart' AND child_code IN
          ('casementSashPart', 'mullionPart', 'transomPart', 'cillPart'))
   OR  (parent_code = 'casementSashPart' AND child_code = 'glassPart')
ORDER  BY parent_code, child_code;

-- 0d. What is in the group today, and that 72-78 are free. Expect the four
--     Step AV templates at 45 / 50 / 60 / 70, the two French casements at
--     80 / 90, and NOTHING between 71 and 79.
SELECT name, group_name, window_type, sort_order, is_active
FROM   public.drawing_templates
WHERE  group_name = 'Combination Flush Casements'
    OR sort_order BETWEEN 71 AND 79
ORDER  BY sort_order;

-- 0e. The product option, and that each new name is free (there is no unique
--     index on name, so a duplicate would be two rows, not an error). Expect
--     one 'Casement' product row and NO rows from the second query.
SELECT code, label, sort_order FROM public.reference_options
WHERE  category = 'product' AND is_active ORDER BY sort_order;

SELECT name, sort_order FROM public.drawing_templates
WHERE  name IN ('Opener, Fixed, Opener (Configuration 4)',
                'Opener, Two Fixed, Opener (Configuration 5)',
                'Openers Either Side Of A Fanlight Over Fixed (Configuration 6)',
                'Three Casements With A Light Over Each (Configuration 7)');


-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- SECTION 1 — the four templates
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

BEGIN;

DO $$
